@title Frontend Framework for the Scheduling Admin Rewrite
@subtitle Comparison from the Internal Tools guild, Wrenfield University IT
@author Internal Tools guild

The course-scheduling admin app is about 60 screens, mostly forms and tables, and five developers will build the rewrite. Three frameworks are in scope: React, Vue and Svelte.

## Criteria

- Team familiarity
- Form and table libraries
- Hiring pool
- Bundle size
- Long-term support

## Comparison

table = Framework,Team familiarity,Form/table ecosystem,Bundle size (KB),Hiring pool; React,4 of 5 developers,excellent,142,large; Vue,1 of 5 developers,good,98,medium; Svelte,0 of 5 developers,fair,41,small

## Pros and cons

### React

**Pros**

- Four of the five developers already know it.
- The data grid we need exists today.
- Large hiring pool.

**Cons**

- Largest bundle of the three, at 142 KB.

### Vue

**Pros**

- Smaller bundle, at 98 KB.
- Good form and table ecosystem.

**Cons**

- Only one developer knows it.
- Medium hiring pool.

### Svelte

**Pros**

- Smallest bundle, at 41 KB.
- Was the favorite in the prototype spike.

**Cons**

- None of the five developers knows it yet.
- Small hiring pool.

## Recommendation

! React, mainly because four of the five developers already know it and the data grid we need exists today.

> We are optimizing for the next five years of maintenance, not the first five weeks of building.
> — Hannah Osei, guild lead

Svelte was the favorite in the prototype spike, and we will revisit it for smaller tools.
